<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41558" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕvēlātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		revelo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an uncovering</i>, <i>laying bare</i>
			(eccl. Lat.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pudendorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 5, 182</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">imaginariae revelationes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aug. Conf. 9, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">filii sui,</span>”
				<i>a revelation</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 5, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vulg. 1 Cor. 1, 7</span></i>. — 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Esp.,</span>”
				<i>the Revelation of St. John</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Lact. Inst. Epit. 42, 8</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
